# ==============================================================================
# 🎾 Wilson Tennis Project - Git Ignore Rules
# ==============================================================================
# This file tells Git which files and directories to ignore in the project.
# Ignoring certain files is crucial to keep the repository clean, secure,
# and free of unnecessary bloat.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Dependencies & Package Managers
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# We ignore node_modules because it contains all the installed packages for the 
# project. These can be massive and should be generated locally using `npm install`.
node_modules/

# We ignore alternative package manager lock files to enforce consistency. 
# Assuming this project uses `package-lock.json` (npm), we ignore yarn and pnpm lock files.
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Environment Variables & Secrets
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERY IMPORTANT: Never commit .env files! They contain sensitive secrets like
# API keys, database passwords (e.g., MONGO_URI), and JWT secrets. 
# Committing these can lead to serious security breaches.
.env
.env.local

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. System & OS Generated Files
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS generates .DS_Store files in directories to store custom attributes
# like folder view options. They are useless to other developers and clutter the repo.
.DS_Store

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Logs & Debugging
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore all log files generated by the application or npm. These change constantly
# and are only relevant to the local environment where the app is running.
logs
*.log

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Build Artifacts
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When the frontend is built for production, the bundled files are placed in these
# directories. We only commit source code, not the generated production bundles,
# as the build step will be run on the deployment server (e.g., Vercel/Render).
dist/
build/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Generated Documentation
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These files might be auto-generated or kept locally as scratchpads. We ignore
# them to prevent overriding the remote version or committing temporary notes.
PROJECT_DOCUMENTATION.md
